{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04MA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\alpha \\star \\text{id}_c = (\\alpha \\star \\text{id}_{\\text{pr}_0}) \\circ\n(\\alpha \\star \\text{id}_{\\text{pr}_1})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi \\circ s \\circ \\text{pr}_1 = \\pi \\circ s \\circ c$", "MATH_0003": "$\\pi \\circ t \\circ \\text{pr}_1 = \\pi \\circ s \\circ \\text{pr}_0$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi \\circ t \\circ \\text{pr}_0 = \\pi \\circ t \\circ c$", "MATH_0005": "$\\circ$", "MATH_0006": "$2$", "MATH_0007": "$[U/_{\\!p}R]$", "MATH_0008": "$c : R \\times_{s, U, t} R \\to R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-quotient-stack}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:97521be5ac1d4f1163c6b336bc40467173ad5c7198d33b72b98462653eb424b3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2232435de890e92864ef835426766338c1e5887abaeaa2b99c297a03c2f9590d", "source_text": "We make two remarks:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The formula\n<MATH_0001> only makes sense if you realize\nthe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>equalities<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0002>,\n<MATH_0003>, and\n<MATH_0004>. Namely, the second\none implies the vertical composition <MATH_0005> makes sense, and the other\ntwo guarantee the two sides of the formula are <MATH_0006>-morphisms with the\nsame source and target.\n<STRUCT_0003> The reason the lemma holds is that composition in the\ncategory fibred in groupoids <MATH_0007> associated to the presheaf\nin groupoids (<REF_0001>) comes from the composition\nlaw <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nWe omit the proof of the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4df86d5f029215f74b7c0ca6e6b79dc7bb248969a9679b5c3fead5341cece892", "un